      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "hate_symbol",
      "label": "Hate Symbol",
      "description": "The swastika is widely recognized as a hate symbol, particularly in the context of anti-Semitism and white supremacist movements. Its use in public gatherings is intended to intimidate, provoke, or glorify hate. Understanding this requires knowledge of how symbols are used to convey political messages and incite hatred.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
